WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.379
Coding tutorials show you the code for a few seconds, then it's gone.

2
00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:05.949
Freezeframe keeps it.

3
00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:11.582
Press the Freeze button in the player, or Alt, Shift, F, on any video.

4
00:00:12.182 --> 00:00:14.600
Drag a box around just the code you want.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.340
Freezeframe reads it on your computer, rebuilds the indentation, and gives you real text.

6
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.280
Shaky spots are highlighted for a double check.

7
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.937
Copy it, edit it, or download it as a file.

8
00:00:27.537 --> 00:00:28.878
Want a second opinion?

9
00:00:29.078 --> 00:00:30.746
Turn on AI assist.

10
00:00:30.946 --> 00:00:37.859
It can fix misreads, explain the code, or make it better, and you always see the suggestion before anything changes.

11
00:00:38.459 --> 00:00:42.840
Here it explains what the code does, and even spots the missing error handling.

12
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.840
Your video frames never leave your computer.

13
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:51.613
AI is off until you turn it on, and with a free local model, nothing leaves your machine at all.

14
00:00:52.213 --> 00:00:54.363
Freezeframe, from Forgeline.

15
00:00:54.563 --> 00:00:56.433
Free, and open source.

16
00:00:56.633 --> 00:00:57.553
Forge ahead.

